// Real anatomical brain meshes for the 3D explorer (ES module, plain arrays).
//
// Sources (fetched from TemplateFlow, https://templateflow.s3.amazonaws.com/):
//  * Cortex (cortexL/R = pial, whiteL/R = grey/white boundary): FreeSurfer fsaverage surfaces,
//      10k density (fsaverage5), tpl-fsaverage/tpl-fsaverage_hemi-{L,R}_den-10k_{pial,white}.surf.gii
//      License: FreeSurfer Software License (free for research/non-commercial use),
//      https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/fswiki/FreeSurferSoftwareLicense ; Fischl et al. 1999.
//  * Subcortical, ventricles, brainstem, cerebellum, corpus callosum: FreeSurfer 'aseg'
//      segmentation of the ICBM 152 Nonlinear Asymmetric 2009c template (MNI152NLin2009cAsym), 1 mm,
//      tpl-MNI152NLin2009cAsym/tpl-MNI152NLin2009cAsym_res-01_seg-aseg_dseg.nii.gz
//      License: (c) 1993-2004 Louis Collins, MNI/McGill - free to use, copy, modify, distribute for
//      any purpose with the copyright notice retained ("as is", no warranty). Fonov et al. 2011.
//
// Processing: subcortical labels -> gaussian(sigma 0.8-1.0 vox) -> marching cubes -> quadric
// decimation -> Taubin smoothing. Cortex: quadric decimation of the pial and white surfaces to 7500 tris/hemi.
// fsaverage is not in MNI152 space; the pial and white surfaces were fitted with a per-axis affine
// (scale 1.039, 1.035, 1.050 in R/A/S) onto the bounding box of the aseg cerebrum labels
// (2,3,41,42), so the cortex encloses the MNI-space subcortical meshes; the same affine is applied to
// the white surfaces so whiteL/R nest inside cortexL/R. Subcortical geometry is
// unmodified MNI152NLin2009cAsym anatomy.
//
// Coordinates: right-handed, x = subject's left->right (+x right), y = up (superior),
// z = anterior (+z front). Centered on the cortex bounding-box center; uniform scale so the
// cortex spans 3.6 units front-to-back (0.02001 units per mm). 3-decimal floats.
// Faces: 0-based triangle indices, counter-clockwise => outward normals (verified by signed volume).
//
// Label ids used (FreeSurfer aseg): thalamus 10/49, caudate 11/50, putamen 12/51, pallidum 13/52,
// hippocampus 17/53, amygdala 18/54, accumbens 26/58, ventralDC 28/60 (contains substantia nigra),
// lateral ventricle 4+5/43+44, 3rd ventricle 14, 4th ventricle 15, brainstem 16,
// cerebellum 7+8+46+47, corpus callosum 251-255.
